.el .ds Aq '
.TH tapectl-cartridge-journal 1  "tapectl-cartridge-journal " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-cartridge\-journal \- Show the MAM journal: every MAM read taken of a cartridge, verbatim
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl cartridge journal\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-serial\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-raw\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIBARCODE\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show the MAM journal: every MAM read taken of a cartridge, verbatim
.PP
ADR\-0013 / issue #297: every `sg_read_attr` a command runs is kept whole — including the attributes tapectl does not parse, such as the medium\*(Aqs own ring of the last four drives that loaded it — because loading the cartridge overwrites them. Lists the rows, oldest first; `\-\-raw <ID>` prints one row\*(Aqs tool output exactly as captured.
.PP
A cartridge\*(Aqs rows are found two ways: reads taken in a contact attributed to it, and reads whose chip serial is its confirmed serial — so a read taken before it was registered is found too. With neither a barcode nor `\-\-serial`, every row is listed, including reads no cartridge could be named for. Read\-only.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-serial\fR \fI<SERIAL>\fR
Select by the medium serial the chip reported instead (for a cartridge that is not registered)
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes. Commands that cannot preview refuse the flag rather than ignore it (issue #241)
.TP
\fB\-\-raw\fR \fI<ID>\fR
Print this journal row\*(Aqs raw `sg_read_attr` output, byte for byte
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip ADR\-0008 Tier\-2 confirmation prompts. It never reaches a Tier\-3 refusal — those are facts, not risks to accept (issue #147)
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file.

NOTE: on its own this ALSO relocates the whole tapectl home to the config file\*(Aqs parent directory — database, keys, staging, receipts. That is how every test harness gets an isolated home, so it still works, but it is surprising enough that it now warns. Use \-\-home when you mean "operate on a different archive", and \-\-config only to point at a config file inside that home (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
tapectl home directory: database, keys, catalogs, receipts, logs.

Defaults to ~/.tapectl. The config file is taken from <home>/config.toml unless \-\-config overrides it. Also settable as TAPECTL_HOME (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
[\fIBARCODE\fR]
Barcode of a registered cartridge
